poe-fan-hat-oled (1.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Show the board's estimated power draw in watts after the fan speed, read
    from the Pi 5 PMIC through the firmware mailbox (OLED_POWER=0 hides it).
    The figure covers the board only: USB devices, the fan, the HAT and
    conversion losses are not included.

 -- Angel Sotirov <angel.sotirov@gmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200

poe-fan-hat-oled (1.0.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Replaces the Seengreat reference demo (numpy + smbus,
    IP found by connecting to 8.8.8.8, run by hand, never installed) with a
    standard-library daemon: SSD1316 over i2c-dev, status from /proc and /sys
    (hostname, uptime, management IPv4, CPU temperature, fan rpm), throttle
    flags from the firmware mailbox and held for a minute, two double-height
    lines per page, burn-in pixel shift, blank on stop, retry instead of
    crash-loop when the bus or panel is missing.
  * Hardened systemd unit: DynamicUser, device access limited to i2c and
    /dev/vcio, IPAddressDeny=any.

 -- Angel Sotirov <angel.sotirov@gmail.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0200
